BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-182100@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260508T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Finding Justice with New England Innocence Project
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 8 spots left
 \nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/18
 2100\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nAn evening that will challen
 ge what you think you know about justice - and redefine what it means to r
 ebuild a life.\n\nHear firsthand from Sean Ellis and Edward Wright—two m
 en who were wrongfully convicted\, spent decades incarcerated\, and ultima
 tely fought to reclaim their freedom. Their stories are deeply personal\, 
 but also powerful reflections on systemic failure\, resilience\, and the l
 ong road to exoneration.\n\nSean Ellis\, whose case gained international a
 ttention through the Netflix docuseries Trial 4\, now leads advocacy effo
 rts through the Exoneree Network\, supporting others navigating life after
  incarceration. Edward Wright\, exonerated after 41 years\, taught himself
  the law while imprisoned - successfully fighting for his own freedom whil
 e helping others do the same.\n\nThe conversation will be guided by Radha 
 Natarajan\, Executive Director of the New England Innocence Project\, whos
 e work continues to confront bias and drive meaningful reform within the j
 ustice system.\n\nA rare opportunity to engage with voices at the forefron
 t of justice reform - and to witness the strength\, clarity\, and humanity
  behind these extraordinary journeys.\n\n*This event is complimentary and 
 reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182100
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
