BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-184208@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260518T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260518T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260518T190000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Love & Other Monsters" with Emily Frank
 lin
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184208\n\nBookmark the date fo
 r a captivating conversation exploring Love & Other Monsters by Emily Fra
 nklin—a richly imagined novel set against the haunting backdrop of the �
 ��Year Without Summer.”\n\nIn 1816\, amid unrelenting storms on the shor
 es of Lake Geneva\, a group of young literary icons—including Mary and P
 ercy Shelley and the infamous Lord Byron—gather to create\, provoke\, an
 d unravel. At the center of it all is Claire Clairmont: clever\, passionat
 e\, and often overshadowed\, yet determined to carve out her own identity 
 in a world dominated by brilliance and ego. As romance\, rivalry\, and amb
 ition collide\, Claire must navigate loyalty\, longing\, and the cost of l
 iving—and loving—on the edge of history.\n\nBlending historical intrig
 ue with emotional depth\, Love & Other Monsters explores the origins of l
 egendary works like Frankenstein while giving voice to the woman too often
  left out of the story.\n\nJoin us for an engaging discussion moderated by
  Wendy Dodson\, owner of Hummingbird Books\, as we delve into this atmosph
 eric novel and its themes of creativity\, fame\, and the monsters we make�
 ��both real and imagined.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for
  members only. Light refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184208
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
