UID:quin-event-184947@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260521T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T183000
SUMMARY:Rethinking Women's Health: The Head & The Heart
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 1 spot 
 left\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/event
 s/184947\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nThe third installment 
 in our Women’s Health Series explores the powerful and often underexamin
 ed connection between cardiovascular and brain health—two systems deeply
  intertwined in shaping how we live\, age\, and thrive\n\nThis thoughtfull
 y curated conversation brings together two leading physicians whose work r
 eflects both the science and the human experience of health. Dr. Ami Bhatt
 —Chief Innovation Officer at the American College of Cardiology and Chai
 r of the FDA Digital Health Advisory Committee—will explore the “heart
 ” of the conversation\, offering insight into cardiovascular health\, in
 novation\, and the evolving tools shaping prevention and care.\n\nCompleme
 nting this perspective\, Dr. Julia Loewenthal—Assistant Professor of Med
 icine at Harvard Medical School and a board-certified internist and geriat
 rician—will guide the “head” of the discussion\, focusing on brain h
 ealth\, aging\, and the ways cognitive conditions such as dementia uniquel
 y impact women.\n\nDesigned to inform and empower\, this program invites a
  more expansive understanding of women’s health—one that recognizes th
 e deep interconnection between heart\, mind\, and longevity.\n\n*This even
 t is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bite
 s will be served\, and beverages will be available for purchase.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184947
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
